 late night experts  and experts consulted by the rap  o'brien reasoned in bill carter's book  the war for late night that  nbc could have only decided the show was  unprofitable if they factored in  construction of new offices and sets  which is a stretch to say the least  strangers with candy frequently appears  on list of shows cancelled too soon  running for 30 episodes between 1999 and  2000  the show had a murderous row of comedic  talent amy sedaris stephen colbert  paul dinello and janine garofalo and a  strong  cult following fans rejoiced when a  prequel film came out in 2005 starring  all the original cast  during the press store sedaris revealed  something that didn't get much attention  then nor has it since the show was never  cancelled at all  in an interview with the austin  chronicle sedera stated that at no point  was the show ever cancelled  we wanted to go out we wanted a final  episode because usually comedy central  does  things in three seasons so we kind of  figured we had three seasons  we thought if we were going to do it  again yeah we could write 10 episodes or  not write 10 episodes  they just stopped making episodes  figuring that their time  was up anyway the wonder years came to a  natural conclusion  both in the show's continuity and with  real life circumstances  in the show kevin and winnie's  relationship comes to a passionate close  and everyone is ready to move on to  their next chapter  in real life all the young actors were  getting older and the show had to wrap  up sooner  rather than later but according to at  least one source these aren't the true  reasons the show ended the blame lies  with a lawsuit  my hunch was that my father would not  let being called a brainwashed [ __ ] at  his dinner table go by  unremarked during the final season the  show's former costume designer monique  long  filed a sexual harassment suit against  stars fred savage and jason herbie  claiming she was let go from the show  after rebuffing thei